arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini: attach the GPU's four shader-core domains

power-domains named only MT6797_POWER_DOMAIN_MFG, the GPU top. That
powers the L2 and leaves all four shader cores gated at the SPM, so
SHADER_PWRON never acks and panfrost logs "error powering up gpu shader"
on every resume.

List the core domains instead, with power-domain-names, which is what
panfrost's multi-domain attach path consumes — the same shape mt8183 uses
(it also lists only its core domains). MFG and MFG_ASYNC still come up:
they are the cores' parents in the scpsys subdomain hierarchy.

Pairs with gpu/0004 and pmdomain/0006.

Signed-off-by: mratan <mattdratan@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda.dts
@@ -1924,7 +1924,20 @@
 		clocks = <&mfgcfg CLK_MFGCFG_BG3D>;
 		clock-names = "core";
 		mali-supply = <&vgpu>;
-		power-domains = <&scpsys MT6797_POWER_DOMAIN_MFG>;
+		/*
+		 * The four shader-core domains, not the MFG top. Powering only
+		 * MFG (as this node did until 2026-08-21) brings up the L2 and
+		 * nothing else: the cores stay gated at the SPM, SHADER_PWRON
+		 * never acks, and panfrost logs "error powering up gpu shader"
+		 * on every resume. MFG and MFG_ASYNC come along anyway — they
+		 * are the cores' parents in the scpsys subdomain hierarchy.
+		 * Same shape as mt8183, which lists only its core domains.
+		 */
+		power-domains = <&scpsys MT6797_POWER_DOMAIN_MFG_CORE0>,
+				<&scpsys MT6797_POWER_DOMAIN_MFG_CORE1>,
+				<&scpsys MT6797_POWER_DOMAIN_MFG_CORE2>,
+				<&scpsys MT6797_POWER_DOMAIN_MFG_CORE3>;
+		power-domain-names = "core0", "core1", "core2", "core3";
 		operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table>;
 	};
 };
